1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,943
Are you one of those people who never asks

2
00:00:02,943 --> 00:00:06,656
anyone for help and wants to handle everything alone?

3
00:00:06,656 --> 00:00:08,862
And are you proud of it? I am going to tell

4
00:00:08,862 --> 00:00:11,016
you something that may feel uncomfortable.

5
00:00:11,016 --> 00:00:14,102
This is often the same fear other people

6
00:00:14,102 --> 00:00:16,416
carry, only turned inside out.

7
00:00:16,416 --> 00:00:19,187
Two children may grow up in the same home,

8
00:00:19,187 --> 00:00:22,023
with the same love that disappeared without

9
00:00:22,023 --> 00:00:23,936
warning and felt unavailable.

10
00:00:24,176 --> 00:00:26,941
One becomes an adult who checks whether

11
00:00:26,941 --> 00:00:30,131
someone is still there. The other decides she

12
00:00:30,131 --> 00:00:31,336
will need no one,

13
00:00:31,336 --> 00:00:33,936
because needing someone has always hurt.

14
00:00:33,936 --> 00:00:37,332
Both are protecting themselves. One protects

15
00:00:37,332 --> 00:00:41,576
herself by staying close, and the other by moving away.

16
00:00:41,576 --> 00:00:44,448
That is why depending on someone can cause

17
00:00:44,448 --> 00:00:45,816
physical discomfort.

18
00:00:45,816 --> 00:00:49,541
It is not merely an opinion. Your body learned

19
00:00:49,541 --> 00:00:52,456
that support can mean pain and risk.

20
00:00:52,456 --> 00:00:55,340
I talk about these patterns here every day,

21
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:59,096
always looking at the root rather than only the symptom.

22
00:00:59,096 --> 00:01:02,066
If this makes sense to you, follow me so you

23
00:01:02,066 --> 00:01:03,416
can understand more.

24
00:01:03,416 --> 00:01:06,977
And send this to the friend who proudly

25
00:01:06,977 --> 00:01:12,456
handles everything alone and never asks anyone for anything.

